<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n61888" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάξ</span></b> , Adv.
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>with the foot</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐν στήθεσι βὰς ἐξέσπασε μείλινον
					ἔγχος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Il.
					6.65
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				16.503
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. προσβάς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					5.620
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				16.863
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ποδὶ κινήσας</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					10.158
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Od.
				15.45
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἔνθορεν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					17.233
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. δ᾽ ἐφ᾽ ὁρκίοις ἔβη</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Archil.
					<u>Supp.</u>
					2.13
				</span></i>
			; so later 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βοῦς μοι ἐπὶ γλώσσης κρατερῷ ποδὶ λ.
					ἐπιβαίνων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Thgn.
					815
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐπίβα δήμῳ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					847
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. πατεῖσθαι</span> (cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λάγδην</span>) to be trodden <i>under
			foot</i>, <i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Eu.</u>
				110
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ch.</u>
				644
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀθέῳ ποδὶ λ. ἀτίσαι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Eu.</u>
					542
				</span></i>
			 (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λ. ἐπορούσας πλῆξε</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					A.R.
					2.106
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">παίει τε λ. πύξ</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philem.
					1.6
				</span></i>
			
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
			</span></i>: also in late Prose, <i><span class="en">
				Luc.
				<u>Asin.</u>
				31
			</span></i>, al.:—for the form cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">γνύξ, πύξ, ὀδάξ</span>.</div>
